class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> each pole nearly cancels its zero, so the response returns to 1; only near <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> does the zero win. The gain <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span> normalises the DC gain to 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Width</strong>: the −3 dB bandwidth is approximately</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.113em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>So <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.95</span></span></span></span> at 1 kHz gives 16 Hz, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.99</span></span></span></span> gives 3.2 Hz. A narrower notch removes less of the neighbouring signal, but needs the frequency to be known accurately and stable, and it rings for longer, about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> seconds.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"notch\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A 120 Hz notch at 1 kHz. Pull the pole radius toward 1 and the notch narrows; the depth at exactly 120 Hz is always infinite.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A gimbal has a structural resonance at 120 Hz that a 1 kHz control loop excites.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">120/1000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.754</span></span></span></span> rad/sample, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\">cos</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ω</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3011em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.7290</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>With <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.95</span></span></span></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">a</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1.3850</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9025</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">b</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">∝</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1.4579</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Bandwidth: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">0.05</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1000</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">15.9</span></span></span></span> Hz.</li>\n<li>Depth at 120 Hz is infinite on paper and limited by coefficient rounding in practice. At ±1 Hz it is still 18 dB and at ±2 Hz 12 dB; at 100 Hz the loss is only 0.6 dB. The resonance drifts with temperature and payload, so don’t make it too narrow.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">notch.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> scipy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> signal\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">notch</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">f0, fs, r</span>):\n    w0 = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * f0 / fs\n    b = np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.cos(w0), <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>])\n    a = np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * r * np.cos(w0), r * r])\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> b * (a.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>() / b.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>()), a                     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># unity gain at DC</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">gain_db</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">b, a, f, fs</span>):\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=[f], fs=fs)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span> * np.log10(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(H[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-300</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">bandwidth</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">b, a, fs, f0</span>):\n    f = np.linspace(f0 - <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, f0 + <span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">120_001</span>)\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=f, fs=fs)\n    below = f[np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(H) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>**-<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>]\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> below.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - below.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>()\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    fs, f0, r = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1000.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">120.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.95</span>\n    b, a = notch(f0, fs, r)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(a, [<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.38504</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9025</span>], atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-5</span>)\n    depth = gain_db(b, a, f0, fs)\n    bw = bandwidth(b, a, fs, f0)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;depth at 120 Hz <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{depth:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>f}</span> dB, -3 dB width <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{bw:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> Hz (estimate <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>-r)*fs/np.pi:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span>), at 100 Hz <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{gain_db(b, a, <span class=\"hljs-number\">100</span>, fs):<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> dB&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> depth &lt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(bw - (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - r) * fs / np.pi) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> gain_db(b, a, <span class=\"hljs-number\">121</span>, fs) &lt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">15</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> gain_db(b, a, <span class=\"hljs-number\">122</span>, fs) &lt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> gain_db(b, a, <span class=\"hljs-number\">10</span>, fs) &gt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># scipy&#x27;s iirnotch with Q = f0 / bandwidth gives (nearly) the same filter</span>\n    bs, as_ = signal.iirnotch(f0, f0 / ((<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - r) * fs / np.pi), fs=fs)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(as_, a, atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-3</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># remove a 120 Hz resonance riding on a 5 Hz signal</span>\n    t = np.arange(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4000</span>) / fs\n    x = np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span> * t) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span> * np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * <span class=\"hljs-number\">120</span> * t)\n    y = signal.lfilter(b, a, x)\n    resid = y[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:] - np.sin(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span> * t[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>:])\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(resid).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.02</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>The resonance moves from 120 to 126 Hz as the payload changes. Your notch has <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.99</span></span></span></span>. What happens?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The bandwidth is only 3.2 Hz, so at 126 Hz the notch gives little attenuation: the resonance comes back. Widen it (<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.95</span></span></span></span>), track the frequency and retune, or use two notches.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why does a narrow notch ring for a long time after a transient?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Its poles are close to the unit circle, at radius <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span></span></span>, so their response decays like <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. At <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.99</span></span></span></span> that’s a time constant of about 100 samples, 0.1 s at 1 kHz.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p08-l08\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"zeros-on-the-circle-poles-just-inside","title":"Zeros on the circle, poles just inside"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p08-l08-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Approximate −3 dB width in Hz for r = 0.95 at f_s = 1 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(1 − r) f_s/π.</p>\n","answer":15.915,"tol":0.002,"unit":"Hz"},{"id":"p08-l08-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>The coefficient a₂ for r = 0.95?</p>\n","explain":"<p>r².</p>\n","answer":0.9025,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l08-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>The zeros of a notch filter are placed…</p>\n","explain":"<p>For complete cancellation.</p>\n","options":["inside the unit circle","at the origin","on the unit circle at ±ω₀","at z = 1"],"answer":2},{"id":"p08-l08-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Normalised frequency ω₀ in rad/sample for 120 Hz at 1 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>2πf₀/f_s.</p>\n","answer":0.75398,"tol":0.001,"unit":"rad/sample"},{"id":"p08-l08-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>Moving the poles closer to the unit circle makes the notch…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Smaller bandwidth, slower decay.</p>\n","options":["shallower at ω₀","unstable immediately","narrower, with longer ringing","wider"],"answer":2},{"id":"p08-l08-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Approximate decay time constant in samples of poles at r = 0.99?</p>\n","explain":"<p>rⁿ = e^(n ln r).</p>\n","answer":99.5,"tol":0.01,"unit":"samples"}],"code":[{"file":"notch.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\nfrom scipy import signal\n\ndef notch(f0, fs, r):\n    w0 = 2 * np.pi * f0 / fs\n    b = np.array([1, -2 * np.cos(w0), 1.0])\n    a = np.array([1, -2 * r * np.cos(w0), r * r])\n    return b * (a.sum() / b.sum()), a                     # unity gain at DC\n\ndef gain_db(b, a, f, fs):\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=[f], fs=fs)\n    return 20 * np.log10(np.abs(H[0]) + 1e-300)\n\ndef bandwidth(b, a, fs, f0):\n    f = np.linspace(f0 - 60, f0 + 60, 120_001)\n    _, H = signal.freqz(b, a, worN=f, fs=fs)\n    below = f[np.abs(H) < 2**-0.5]\n    return below.max() - below.min()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    fs, f0, r = 1000.0, 120.0, 0.95\n    b, a = notch(f0, fs, r)\n    assert np.allclose(a, [1, -1.38504, 0.9025], atol=1e-5)\n    depth = gain_db(b, a, f0, fs)\n    bw = bandwidth(b, a, fs, f0)\n    print(f\"depth at 120 Hz {depth:.0f} dB, -3 dB width {bw:.2f} Hz (estimate {(1-r)*fs/np.pi:.2f}), at 100 Hz {gain_db(b, a, 100, fs):.2f} dB\")\n    assert depth < -30 and abs(bw - (1 - r) * fs / np.pi) < 1.0\n    assert gain_db(b, a, 121, fs) < -15 and gain_db(b, a, 122, fs) < -12 and gain_db(b, a, 10, fs) > -0.1\n    # scipy's iirnotch with Q = f0 / bandwidth gives (nearly) the same filter\n    bs, as_ = signal.iirnotch(f0, f0 / ((1 - r) * fs / np.pi), fs=fs)\n    assert np.allclose(as_, a, atol=5e-3)\n    # remove a 120 Hz resonance riding on a 5 Hz signal\n    t = np.arange(4000) / fs\n    x = np.sin(2 * np.pi * 5 * t) + 0.5 * np.sin(2 * np.pi * 120 * t)\n    y = signal.lfilter(b, a, x)\n    resid = y[1000:] - np.sin(2 * np.pi * 5 * t[1000:])\n    assert np.abs(resid).max() < 0.02"}]}